<section class="section section--proof shell" aria-labelledby="semantic-title">
  <div class="section-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span>Not just boxes</span> The model is the product</p>
    <h2 id="semantic-title">Your diagrams should understand what they describe.</h2>
    <p>
      Drawing tools see shapes. ArchLex sees cloud resources, boundaries, and typed relationships—so the diagram can tell you when the architecture does not add up.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="semantic-comparison">
    <article class="comparison-panel comparison-panel--muted">
      <div class="comparison-panel__label">A drawing tool</div>
      <div class="generic-diagram" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>BOX</span><i>→</i><span>BOX</span><i>→</i><span>BOX</span>
      </div>
      <p>Everything is a rectangle. Every connection is accepted.</p>
      <div class="comparison-status">No semantic context</div>
    </article>
    <article class="comparison-panel comparison-panel--signal">
      <div class="comparison-panel__label">An ArchLex diagram</div>
      <img
        class="semantic-diagram"
        src="/diagrams/serverless-api.svg"
        alt="API Gateway invokes Lambda which writes to DynamoDB"
        width="742"
        height="116"
      />
      <p>Provider rules validate containment and relationship compatibility.</p>
      <div class="comparison-status"><b>✓</b> Architecture valid</div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
